cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "distributed-mpc-admm: Distributed MPC via consensus ADMM"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Eiman
    given-names: "M. Ali"
    email: ali.eimaan@icloud.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/Ali-Eiman/distributed-mpc-admm"
abstract: >-
  A distributed model-predictive controller for double-integrator agents in 2D,
  coupled only through formation costs and solved by general-form consensus ADMM
  over a communication graph. Ships a readable Python reference and a real-time
  C++/ROS 2 kernel (OSQP, one process per agent) that are pinned to each other by
  an iterate-level parity test, together with the derivations and the experiments
  that measure where the standard convergence guarantee stops applying.
keywords:
  - model predictive control
  - distributed optimization
  - ADMM
  - consensus
  - multi-agent systems
  - formation control
  - ROS 2
license: BSD-3-Clause
